    {
      "id": "code",
      "kind": "code",
      "lang": "python",
      "source": "def canFinish(n, prereqs):\n    indeg = [0] * n\n    graph = defaultdict(list)\n    for a, b in prereqs:\n        graph[b].append(a)\n        indeg[a] += 1\n    q = deque(i for i in range(n) if indeg[i] == 0)\n    done = 0\n    while q:\n        node = q.popleft()\n        done += 1\n        for nxt in graph[node]:\n            indeg[nxt] -= 1\n            if indeg[nxt] == 0:\n                q.append(nxt)\n    return done == n"
    },
    {
      "id": "ctext",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Why it's fast",
      "body": [
        "Each course and each arrow is handled once → O(V + E)",
        "The queue and indegree array hold V entries → O(V) space"
      ],
      "variant": "bullets"
    },
    {
      "id": "otext",
      "kind": "text",
      "body": [
        "If the queue empties early,",
        "something is waiting on itself."
      ],
      "variant": "big"
    }
